    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 698 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-joyeong">Dae Joyeong</a>, who led Goguryeo refugees and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohe">Mohe</a> tribesmen after the fall of Goguryeo.</li><li>It ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> from Tang-style capitals such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanggyeong">Sanggyeong</a>, modelled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>.</li><li>Conquered by the Khitan in 926, it is claimed in Korean history as the northern partner of Unified Silla.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Tang <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xuanming-calendar">Xuanming calendar</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> used for more than 800 years from 862, first reached Japan with an embassy from Balhae.</p></aside>
    </section>

